<title>USA: No sign of penetrating cold for Brazil coffee -- WSC.</title>
<headline>No sign of penetrating cold for Brazil coffee -- WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colder air expected to build into Central Argentina next week does not appear strong enough right now to penetrate northward into Brazil's coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Thursday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed over main growing areas of the belt this morning. Temperatures remained near normal levels for this time of year. Lows this morning were in the 50's F (low to middle teens C). Some cooler conditions were reported in higher elevations.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next 5-7 days. Temperatures should remain near to above normal. Lows will be in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>There is still no damaging cold expected, according to WSC. ((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
